<p>US Vice President JD Vance traveled to Budapest on April 7 to publicly back Prime Minister Viktor Orbán and his Fidesz party just days before Hungary’s parliamentary election on April 12. Appearing with Orbán at a rally, Vance praised him as a model for Europe and said he and President Trump stood “shoulder to shoulder” with the Hungarian leader. Trump also voiced his support from the United States. The visit gave Hungary’s final days of campaigning an international edge before the April 12 vote. Vance also used the trip to attack the European Union, accusing Brussels of interfering in Hungary’s politics during his remarks in Budapest. The episode underscores both the closeness between the current US administration and Orbán and the importance of the coming vote for Hungary’s direction inside Europe.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/QP_kJ_hWHt9qj4_CCM7I7cS9VZ3qPB4bnlFjJspYn_pYMQCMNBWBNnzQRVaN-Tnsq4qDVUc-SDzmCVn_i0v9_0Xi4vaaM8EgrTGdcqHmO48IphsGRevgtRPMSY5QshCJ9yxDoMasbu6BBuaM6Tc-mJcl1RGOygBJqLOBk6KIrPlnKa0ApnyiqUKrqmqj4y3tCvjS4hmKCVH0e3mY3e72A3UMt5CoGE6CpfKqAsUpWK2qZ27z6pkNNYBrA46oUjoBfJU4QuI2JeabNkQf6Q' alt='U.S. Vice President J.D. Vance and Hungarian Prime Minister Viktor Orbán attend an election campaign rally in Budapest on April 7, 2026, ahead of Hungary’s parliamentary elections.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Poll pressure: The Globe and Mail reported that Fidesz was trailing Tisza by 10 points ahead of Sunday’s election, while The Straits Times said independent polls showed Orbán on track to lose power after 16 years.</li><li>Campaign rally: Vance joined Orbán at an indoor sports arena rally in Budapest, where thousands of cheering supporters turned out during the vice president’s visit.</li><li>Direct intervention: The Guardian reported that Vance said he had come to Budapest to “help” Orbán win, an unusually explicit endorsement by a sitting US vice president in a European election campaign.</li><li>Combative arrival: Shortly after landing, Vance called Brussels’ conduct “one of the worst examples of foreign election interference” he had ever seen.</li></ul><blockquote>Shoulder to shoulder - JD Vance</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>JD Vance: Vance cast the trip as both an endorsement of Orbán and a confrontation with Brussels, arguing that EU bureaucrats had tried to hurt Hungary’s economy and meddle in its election. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/07/jd-vance-eu-interference-hungary-election-viktor-orban'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Viktor Orbán and Hungarian government: Orbán’s government treated the visit as a diplomatic lift, presenting it as proof of especially warm ties with Washington and a possible “new golden age” in bilateral relations. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/07/jd-vance-hungary-viktor-orban-election'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Polling-based view: Independent surveys cited by outlets suggested Tisza still held the lead before the vote, raising doubts that a high-profile American endorsement would be enough to shift the race’s late momentum. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/us-v-p-j-d-vance-picks-fight-with-europe-over-hungarys-orban-in-vote-endorsement'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>US administration: The New York Times portrayed Washington’s message as unusually personal as well as political, with Trump and Vance praising Orbán as a fellow nationalist ally in the campaign’s final days. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/07/world/europe/vance-hungary-orban-fidesz-election.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/07/vance-hails-orban-as-model-for-europe-during-pre-election-visit-to-hungary_6752194_4.html'>Vance hails Orban as &#x27;model&#x27; for Europe during pre-election visit to Hungary</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/us-v-p-j-d-vance-picks-fight-with-europe-over-hungarys-orban-in-vote-endorsement'>US V-P Vance picks fight with Europe over Hungary’s Orban in vote endorsement</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-trump-vance-orban-hungary-election/'>Trump and Vance stump for Orban ahead of Hungarian election</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/news-wrap-vance-backs-orban-in-visit-ahead-of-hungarian-elections'>News Wrap: Vance backs Orbán in visit ahead of Hungarian elections</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/07/jd-vance-hungary-viktor-orban-election'>Vance’s whirlwind visit may not help Orbán to the election victory he craves</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/07/world/europe/vance-hungary-orban-fidesz-election.html'>‘I Love Viktor’: Trump and Vance Cheer on Orban in Hungarian Race</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cyv16lq2rp1o'>JD Vance backs Orbán&#x27;s re-election bid in Budapest visit and hits out at EU</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>